    "narrative": "The path to value today centers on exploiting favorable SP_xERA matchups, headlined by **Geraldo Perdomo** (68.61) and **Tyler Freeman** (68.19). **Geraldo Perdomo** benefits from the most significant SP skill boost of the day against Agnos (5.15 xERA), and despite the slight platoon disadvantage, his elevation to the #3 spot provides the necessary floor to lead our unit. **Tyler Freeman** continues to capitalize on his position atop the order, as his matchup against Ed Rodriguez (4.55 xERA) allows him to leverage his consistent contact profile for a high-efficiency start. While **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (66.66) faces a tougher arm in Mize (3.82 xERA), he remains a must-start given his elite dual-threat profile, even with a minor downgrade due to the opposing catcher\u2019s efficiency in neutralizing stolen base attempts.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved separating **Daulton Varsho** (55.41) from **Lawrence Butler** (55.05). Both represent marginal starts, but **Daulton Varsho** gets the nod due to his high-leverage #3 spot in the order, which mitigates the risk posed by his poor platoon split against Rod\u00f3n. **Lawrence Butler** carries an intriguing 13% boost from a favorable platoon matchup against Soriano, but his position in the #9 slot suppresses his overall scoring potential, effectively capping his utility today. We are monitoring the injury status of **Cal Raleigh** and **Yainer Diaz** closely; their absence continues to pinch our depth, forcing us to lean on **Geraldo Perdomo** and others to fill the void while **Bryson Stott** and **Will Smith** remain unavailable due to the team\u2019s off-day schedule. \n\nGiven the scarcity of stolen bases in our current standings, we are carefully watching **Masyn Winn** (43.36). He faces a significant risk today against Ashcraft, whose ability to suppress running games is bolstered by an elite defensive catcher. If **Masyn Winn** fails to reach base early, his score could bottom out quickly, potentially impacting our weekly game cap strategy. We are otherwise positioned to avoid the \"Below floor\" tier, ensuring that our remaining assets like **Taylor Ward**, **Matt Chapman**, and **Luis Arraez** stay fresh for more opportunistic matchups later in the week.",
